serInfo is more of my domain model.  UserInfo has properties that shouldn't be mapped. \n\nWhen I execute, I'm getting this exception:\n\nException thrown: 'System.ArgumentOutOfRangeException' in AutoMapper.dll\nSystem.ArgumentOutOfRangeException: Cannot find a field or property named Errors\nParameter name: name\n   at AutoMapper.Internal.MappingExpression`2.ForMember(String name, Action`1 memberOptions)\n   at AutoMapper.ConfigurationStore.CreateMappingExpression[TSource,TDestination](TypeMap typeMap)\n   at AutoMapper.ConfigurationStore.CreateMap[TSource,TDestination](String profileName, MemberList memberList)\n   at AutoMapper.ConfigurationStore.CreateMap[TSource,TDestination](String profileName)\n   at AutoMapper.ConfigurationStore.CreateMap[TSource,TDestination]()\n   at AutoMapper.Mapper.CreateMap[TSource,TDestination]()\n   at Xiard.MVVM.Core.CoreDTOManager.InitializeMappings()\n\nThe class hierarchy for UserInfo is UserInfo <- DomainObject <- ModelBase. \n\nModelBase has the following Errors property:\n\n```\n    ObservableCollection<string> _errors = new ObservableCollection<string>();\n    [SQLite.Net.Attributes.Ignore, AutoMapper.IgnoreMap]\n    public ObservableCollection<string> Errors { get { return _errors; } }\n```\n\nFrom the error, it sounds like AutoMapper may be looking for an Errors property on UserInfoDTO (which doesn't exist). But I would have thought the AutoMapper.IgnoreMap attrbute would have taken care of that.\n\nI'm fairly new to AutoMapper, so I don't know if there is something I need to be doing to configure AutoMapper specifically to handle this case.\n\nAny idea what I'm doing wrong?  \n","closed_by":{"login":"jbogard","id":104498,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDQ5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104498?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbogard","html_url":"https://github.com/jbogard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbogard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/u